# R2 — stop computing the exact coefficient rate where a closed form replaces it

date: 2026-08-13
host: mac (Apple aarch64, 12 logical cores), box shared with another agent —
      every timed run wrapped in `~/bin/measlock` (mutual exclusion + wait for
      quiet). NEITHER SIDE NICED.
base: 7dec5f24e (the census commit; behaviourally identical to cb4652c44)
cand: this commit
build: both arms `RUSTFLAGS=-C llvm-args=-align-all-functions=4`, no
       `target-cpu=native`. Control arm = a byte-IDENTICAL SECOND COPY of the
       base binary (`md5` equal), run in the same session on the same grid.
harness: rust/tools/perf_ab.sh — interleaved paired rounds, order randomised
       per round, one untimed warmup inside each sample.
noise floor: the repo's documented identity band is [0.9843, 1.0190]; anything
       inside it is NULL whatever its sign.

## What changed

`tx_unit_inner` used to compute `cost_coeffs_txb` FIRST and then discard it on
the two branches where C's closed forms apply. C's rate tiers are an
`if / else if / else` and the estimator is never reached on those arms
(`product_coding_loop.c:4914-4934`, `:5540-5564`, `:5883-5890`). The port now
evaluates the tiers in C's order.

This is NOT a dead-value elimination and needs no deadness proof: on
`RateMode::Lvl0Closed` `tx_unit` produces the SAME closed form
(`th = (w*h)>>6; eob < th ? 6000+eob*1000 : 3000+eob*100`) from the SAME inputs
(`eob`, `w*h`) that the MDS3 depth loop applies to the result afterwards. The
depth loop's own expression is untouched.

The one place the substituted value is genuinely observed is `txt_search`'s
per-tx-type `cost` compare. That is inert only when exactly one type is
evaluated, so `txt_search` DEMOTES `Lvl0Closed` to `Exact` unless `only_dct`.
`coeff_rate_est_lvl == 0` implies `txt_on == false` implies `only_dct`
(`FunnelCfg::for_preset`'s `_ =>` arm), so the demotion never fires today; it
exists so a future preset table cannot make the search rate-sensitive silently.

## Measured — qp 20 (where the census says R2 fires hardest)

| cell      | n  | R2 ratio | control ratio | verdict |
|-----------|---:|---------:|--------------:|---------|
| 256 p10   | 25 |  0.9461  | 0.9958        | REAL 1.057x |
| 256 p13   | 25 |  0.9438  | 1.0056        | REAL 1.060x |
| 512 p10   | 25 |  0.9539  | 0.9952        | REAL 1.048x |
| 512 p13   | 25 |  0.9519  | 1.0021        | REAL 1.051x |
| 1024 p10  | 25 |  0.9538  | 0.9981        | REAL 1.048x |
| 1024 p13  | 25 |  0.9632  | 1.0013        | REAL 1.038x |

Six of six outside the noise band, all in the same direction; every control
cell inside it. p25/p75 in the TSVs: the R2 arm's p75 (0.958-0.973) never
reaches the control arm's p25 (0.973-0.989), so the distributions are disjoint
at the quartiles, not just at the median.

