## Measured — no regression anywhere R2 does not fire (qp 40, n=9)

p2 / p6 / p7 / p8 at 256 and 512: R2 ratios 0.9965-1.0107, control ratios
0.9933-1.0125. Every cell inside the band on both arms. The reordering adds one
boolean per `tx_unit` call at those presets and costs nothing measurable.

## Why the qp gradient, and the review correction it implies

`benchmarks/txunit_census_2026-08-13.tsv`: the share of `cost_coeffs_txb`
COEFFICIENT work the closed form replaces is 51-54 % at p10/p13 qp20, 16-38 %
at qp40, and **0 % at qp55** (`end_depth == 0` there, so the level-0 closed form
is not on the `perform_tx_partitioning` path at all). The wall-clock tracks that
share, which is the strongest evidence that the win is the mechanism claimed and
not a layout artefact.

The review scoped R2 as "presets >= 9 (level 0) AND presets 7-8 (level 2)". The
level-2 arm is effectively dead: it needs `eob < (w*h)>>6`, which fired on 164
of 8,404 calls in ONE of eighteen p7/p8 cells (328 coefficients in total) and on
zero calls in the other seventeen. It is still landed — it is a branch swap —
but it should be priced at zero, and the p7/p8 rows above confirm that.

## Byte-identity

byteid_fingerprint 168/168, `port_md5 == c_md5` on all 168, and the whole file
`diff`s clean against the pre-change fingerprint. decode_gate_grid 120/120
(aomdec + dav1d, byte-identical to C). partial_sb_gate 146/146. recon_parity
432/432 (199 streams fired CDEF, 118 signalled wiener). Workspace nextest
1029/1029.

## Not done

The bd10 mirror (`tx_unit_hbd` / `TxRdArgs`) still computes the exact rate on
both closed-form branches — same defect, same fix shape, not touched here. It is
reachable only from the bd10 re-encode pass, which none of the gap cells run.
